==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From the {{der|is|non|skyr||thick curdled milk}}<ref>J.Fritzner. Ordbog over det gamle norske Sprog. 1862, Christiania. </ref>. Related to the terms {{m|non|skjör-ost}} in {{w|Funen|Fjón}}, {{w|Denmark}}, {{m|nn|skjør-ost}} or {{m|nn|skjør}} in {{w|Norwegian}}, meaning “buttermilk” or “cultured milk”, and many similar terms in Swedish dialects. The Latin term {{m|la|[[lac]] [[concresco|concretum]]|thick milk}} is in {{w|Germania (book)|the book Germania}} by {{w|Tacitus}}.

